# Historical knowledge baseline and candidate designs

Use this maintained English reference for sections 1–2 of the [frozen Chinese
baseline export](采用基线与候选.md). The [provenance](采用基线与候选.provenance.json)
records the original `知识库设计/需求与设计基线.md`, source digest, and selected
sections. These choices and candidate designs describe the original FormSy
design project. Verify this project's decisions, versions, scope, and
permissions independently. Apply the [shared conventions](共同约定.md) to the
current task.

## 1. Recorded choices in the historical design

| ID | User choice | Historical design boundary |
| --- | --- | --- |
| KBR01 | Support SOP generation and self-check while recording project requirements, designs, and previous decisions. | Keep general reference and project context as distinct roles with their own applicability. |
| KBR02 | Allow manual import and collect system candidates. Adopt reference material through confirmation. | The user selects local sources. Track a separate review state for system candidates and add them to formal context only after adoption. |
| KBR03 | Support documents in the first release and leave code analysis for a later extension. | Exclude source repository, function, and dependency-graph analysis from this release. Retain extension interfaces in parsers and source adapters. |
| KBR04 | Share general material, isolate project material, and require explicit selection for cross-project use. | Enforce scope in retrieval, original reads, context assembly, and exports. |
| KBR05 | Store and retrieve material locally. A configured model API may receive relevant excerpts and citations needed for the task. | Keep remote bulk indexing and whole-library upload outside the default. Actual costs require current authorization and project budget. |
| KBR06 | Deliver the architecture diagram, knowledge SOP, module interfaces, and self-check rules for this historical round. | Deliver reviewable documents and diagrams. Keep FormSyHelper integration, project migration, and model API calls outside that documentation scope. |
| KBR07 | Continue the earlier local-first direction and consider UnderstandAnything as a candidate. | Evaluate existing tools within the document scope. Check actual authorization before adding a dependency, using a service, or installing anything. |
| KBR08 | Confirm the applicable stages and obtain renewed confirmation when requirements, the design, or permissions change. | Record knowledge adoption and stage confirmation independently. A source change leaves the confirmed baseline intact until the applicable decision. |

KBR01–KBR06 came from the original round's individual questions and answers.
KBR07–KBR08 came from earlier explicit choices in the same historical chat.
Use these IDs as source locators. Use actual application approval IDs for
application evidence. A manual import may include explicit adoption for the
selected version and scope in the same operation. Reuse a valid adoption
decision. Apply a valid adoption decision before using a source with no
explicit adoption, including a system candidate, in formal generation.

## 2. Candidate defaults from the historical design

Review each candidate against the current project before adopting it.

| ID | Proposal | Rationale and boundary |
| --- | --- | --- |
| KBD01 | Start with Markdown, TXT, DOCX, and text-based PDF. Save local page-content snapshots after review when applicable. | Validate parsing and locators during implementation. Report limits separately for scanned documents and OCR, encryption, and complex layouts. |
| KBD02 | Use local source snapshots, version and metadata catalogs, and a rebuildable text index. | Preserve source and citation traceability. Confirm the storage technology independently. |
| KBD03 | Start with local full-text search, metadata filters, and ranking as needed. Keep semantic search behind a replaceable adapter. | Establish source and scope accuracy first. Measure retrieval on annotated samples. Keep external vector API calls outside the default. |
| KBD04 | Give a source update a new version and impact list. Use manual refresh as the proposed initial workflow. | Allow comparison and adoption. Keep original confirmation bound to the earlier version. Treat automatic monitoring as a later option. |
| KBD05 | Retrieve from a fixed knowledge snapshot for the stage or object. Supply the model with the minimum relevant excerpts and citations. | Keep the task context reproducible. Use only authorized project material and adopted sources. |
| KBD06 | Check confirmed project decisions and formal rules first. Register conflicts with reference material explicitly. | Triage disagreement between source claims and user requirements. Keep the goal bound to the applicable user decision. Search ranking and majority agreement provide reference signals only. |
| KBD07 | Share general documents. Apply scope filters to project documents and indexes before retrieval. Deduplicate content without merging permissions. | Verify permission and version for original reads and model context as well as retrieval. |
| KBD08 | Record adoption, rule applicability, factual support, stage confirmation, and real tests separately. | Adoption records consent to use the document. Check correctness, applicability, and any requirement separately. |
